{"title":"2015 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 3b","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2015 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A formula for the sum of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> positive integers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/0/8a0e1838843e1cfeecae58c176ab804181f7c966.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 2 + 3 + \\cdots + n = \\frac{n(n + 1)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"246\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>For example, to calculate the sum of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> positive integers, we evaluate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/1/40170f10dc9225443c02dbbfa2a29ef462c65587.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 2 + 3 + 4 = \\frac{4(4 + 1)}{2} = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"239\" height=\"40\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Calculate the sum of the 50 consecutive integers beginning at 151, that is,\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/4/bb4a551c1af8251d35cb28af006a31f33d7fc2df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$151 + 152 + 153 + \\cdots + 198 + 199 + 200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"320\" height=\"15\" /></center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realize that we can pair <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/9/c39f78c92e8eadd503e39d2732305638842deaf4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$151$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/3/8f37626d49b4082c9102bf930bca51277ff2eb43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/5/e457abc5e55d562a8e426b0d19d8d006c9c06ace.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$152$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/3/0f31ff033089cb9cfa5a6ce6cd9a0ce6b5c57422.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$199$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, etc, giving the same sum each time.\n</p><p>Each pair would have a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/3/f53c311077d2cb43b0cff65c978a9a9798469027.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$151 + 200 = 351$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"15\" />. There are also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> consecutive integers, so there would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/f/3df5272791db7e0d6c059e8ffcee664eef09303c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{50}{2} = 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"66\" height=\"38\" /> pairs (since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is even).\n</p><p>This means that the sum would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/e/a8e92876624fce924c6e63e4ba5323bf56adba8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$351 \\times 25 = \\boxed{8775}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"141\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/b/74b387cb82901d107a73d000362488b3d7cd1339.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$151 + 152 + \\cdots + 198 + 199 + 200 = (1 + 2 + 3 + \\cdots + 199 + 200) - (1 + 2 + 3 + \\cdots + 149 + 150)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"774\" height=\"20\" />. since all of the terms from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/e/f5e10e5f3aa7c766cb27c3ad319fa526f71588cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$150$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> will cancel out.\n</p><p>From <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3a\" title=\"2015 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 3a\">part a</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/2/f32f12382bd95e19b134cf82aad214939a94c129.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 2 + 3 + \\cdots + 199 + 200 = 20~100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"291\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Using the formula given in the original problem, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/6/a06bd8444ef0b168dc95988a54f9b63ae0a59f3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 2 + 3 + \\cdots + 149 + 150 = \\frac{150(150 + 1)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"344\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/6/5769de72890633018808fe58c3549adbdcd12beb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=75 \\times 151$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"89\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/1/95107e367413c93742c3049b6072393dd0bc0f88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=11~325$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/9/759355d9cc00584b156d7b777786729592c620a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$151 + 152 + \\cdots + 198 + 199 + 200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"271\" height=\"15\" /> is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/c/2bccb180ef85efc93d9c8c65f7e50aed145da150.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20~100 - 11~325 = \\boxed{8775}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"198\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018000358\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.017 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.032 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 102/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 349/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4413/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.189      1 2015_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3\n100.00%    7.189      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36966:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018000358 and revision id 285857. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}